      {
        "narration": "Every gear inside the ancient Swiss clock reversed direction simultaneously. No sparks flew. No alarms rang out across the quiet medieval square.",
        "visual_query": "bern zytglogge medieval clock tower",
        "visual_fallback": "swiss medieval clock mechanism"
      },
      {
        "narration": "In 1998, technicians at the Zytglogge tower in Bern stripped the iron casing and found zero broken teeth or jammed springs. Every single wheel turned smoothly backward.",
        "visual_query": "antique clock gears mechanism macro",
        "visual_fallback": "metal gears turning close up"
      },
      {
        "narration": "How do hundreds of pounds of interlocking brass and iron unmake their own momentum without breaking a single tooth?",
        "visual_query": "historic clock interior cogs",
        "visual_fallback": "complex clockwork interior"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Detailed diagnostics later revealed that a modern digital motor control system had been covertly retrofitted behind the iron dial.",
        "visual_query": "modern electronic control board wires",
        "visual_fallback": "circuit board macro view"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The impossible reversal was actually an unauthorized artistic stunt pulled by a local horologist. But why did he risk prison just to make time run backward for a single afternoon?",
        "visual_query": "swiss old town cobblestone street",
        "visual_fallback": "european historic town square"
      }
